sequenceDiagram
    participant WC as QWebChannel
    participant JS as chat-bridge.js
    participant CPP as AiBridge (C++)
    participant API as LLM API
    participant DC as deep-chat

    rect rgb(220, 235, 255)
        Note over CPP,WC: INITIALIZATION (page load)
        CPP->>CPP: connect(personaChanged → clearChat)
        CPP->>CPP: connect(provider/model/endpoint/apiKey/extraParams/… → clearChat)
        JS->>WC: DOMContentLoaded → create QWebChannel
        WC-->>JS: expose aiBridge object
        JS->>JS: setupDeepChat()
        JS->>CPP: setTimeout(100ms): clearChat()
    end

    rect rgb(255, 250, 230)
        Note over CPP,DC: INTRO MESSAGE FLOW
        CPP->>CPP: isBusy()? → if yes, set m_deferredClearChat and return
        CPP->>CPP: stopStream()
        CPP->>CPP: clearConversation() (also resets AgentStateTracker baseline)
        CPP-->>JS: emit onClearChat()
        JS->>JS: currentSignals = null
        JS->>DC: clearMessages()
        JS->>DC: addMessage("Starting up…")
        CPP->>CPP: sendIntroMessage()
        Note over CPP: m_conversation.append({role:"user", content:"Give a short introduction."})
        Note over CPP: m_isIntroStream = true
        CPP-->>JS: emit onStreamOpen()
        JS->>JS: _introBuf = ""  (currentSignals is null → intro path)
        CPP->>API: POST /chat/completions (SSE, without tools)
        loop Each SSE chunk
            API-->>CPP: delta: {"content":"Hi!"}
            Note over CPP: processSSEData → merge into m_assistantDelta
            CPP-->>JS: emit onStreamChunk("Hi!")
            JS->>JS: _introBuf += "Hi!"
        end
        API-->>CPP: data: [DONE]
        Note over CPP: onReplyFinished → save assistant msg to m_conversation
        CPP-->>JS: emit onStreamClose()
        JS->>DC: clearMessages()
        JS->>DC: addMessage(_introBuf)
        Note over JS,DC: "Starting up…" replaced with intro text
    end
